    {
      "id": 316945,
      "username": "ALAADIAA",
      "name": "Alaa Alsalehi",
      "created_at": "2022-03-05T08:45:00.500Z",
      "cooked": "<p>really a very good question and here is why we do not go with shipped in ERPNext accounting directly<br>\n1- because we need to have flexibility on the business side let us say we want to allow users to transfer their money from their wallet to a friend’s wallet.<br>\n2- that helps us to automate the cycle from API without needing to know more about customer payments details. The wallet has all payments information it needs to find those payments that do not bind to a sales invoice and bind them to this new unpaid invoice.</p>\n<p>I hope this explain our thinking</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/alaadiaa/{size}/40937_2.png",
      "trust_level": 2,
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 106,
      "wikis": null,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_view_edit_history": true,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "version": 1,
      "last_edited_at": null,
      "edited_at": null
    },
    {
      "id": 317005,
      "username": "Maheshwari_Bhavesh",
      "name": "Bhavesh Maheshwari",
      "created_at": "2022-03-06T06:38:03.525Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I got your idea but you can manage with account itself and not require to manage separate module for that.</p>\n<p>Like you can use journal entry for transfer amount from one wallet to another wallet.  Even there is all validation so chance of mistake very low. Also you can use general ledger report for history of any wallet so you no need to write any custom logic to get history of all wallet, get wallet balance , etc.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/maheshwari_bhavesh/{size}/55067_2.png",
      "trust_level": 4,
